    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1051">

                <pb facs="1295" n="1277" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg1277"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.20233/2–1746</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dawson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-02-22T17:00:00-05:00">February 22, 1946—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>72. Reurtel 110, Feb 17.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d1051-f1"/> You may inform Pres Amezaga that our Ger investigations to date have necessarily been concentrated on
                    sources pertaining directly to Ger-Arg affairs; hence, we do not yet know what
                    documentary and other evidence pertaining directly to Uruguay is available. If
                    you deem it useful you may inform him however that an informed official of the
                        Ger Foreign Office has stated “The SD brought Brinckmann<anchor n="22"
                        xml:id="d1051-f2"/> together with the agent Bove Trabal who functioned as a
                    courier from Uruguay and brought information from there, which information the
                        SD and Brinckmann shared, Brinckmann <pb
                        facs="1296" n="1278" xml:id="pg1278"/> using it for the Arg Army and the SD
                    for Ger.” Blue Book<anchor n="23"
                        xml:id="d1051-f3"/> identifies Brinckmann.</p>
                <p>We will be glad to make available further data as it is uncovered.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1051-f1" n="21" xml:id="d1051-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1051-f2" n="22" xml:id="d1051-f2-content">
                <p>Go-between between Perón and the SD.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1051-f3" n="23" xml:id="d1051-f3-content">
                <p>For documentation on the “Blue Book”, see <ref target="#pg182">pp. 182</ref>
                    ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
